# =============================================================================
# Trivy Ignore File
# Add check IDs here to suppress known/accepted findings.
# Format: AVD-AWS-XXXX, one ID per line with explanation comment.
# =============================================================================

# KMS key policy grants root account full access — required by AWS for key
# administration and break-glass recovery. Already documented in kms.tf.
AVD-AWS-0065
AVD-AWS-0066

# EKS cluster secrets encryption is conditionally enabled via
# var.enable_secrets_encryption. When create_kms_key = false the module uses
# AWS-managed encryption (no CMK block needed). Annotated in main.tf with
# checkov:skip=CKV_AWS_58.
AVD-AWS-0039

# EKS cluster API server endpoint public access is controlled by
# var.endpoint_public_access (default = false). The module defaults to
# private-only access (endpoint_private_access = true, endpoint_public_access = false).
# This finding fires on the variable declaration itself.
AVD-AWS-0040

# EKS cluster control plane logging: all log types are enabled by default
# (api, audit, authenticator, controllerManager, scheduler).
# This finding is suppressed because logging is on by default and controlled
# by var.cluster_logging_enabled + var.enabled_cluster_log_types.
AVD-AWS-0038

# Launch template metadata options: IMDSv2 is enforced by default
# (http_tokens = "required", hop_limit = 2). Annotated in launch_template.tf
# with checkov:skip=CKV_AWS_79 and CKV_AWS_341.
AVD-AWS-0028
AVD-AWS-0130

# EKS node group launch template not specified when create_launch_template = false.
# When the module is used without a launch template (e.g. AWS Academy with LabRole),
# disk_size on the node group covers encryption via AMI defaults.
AVD-AWS-0099
